@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-repeals`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-repeals.l4 (sections 2, 15, 16 and 17 of the Interpretation Act 1978).
--
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and written down before the module was run. A failing assertion is
-- a finding; no expected value is edited to match the code. FALSE in a "provides that" function means the section does not
-- provide it, never that the opposite is the law.

§ `Fixtures: the substituted provisions of section 17(1)`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment`
      d    IS A DATE
      provision IS A `Provision on coming into force`
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`an enactment` kind d provision MEANS `An enactment` WITH
    `its kind`                             IS kind
    `the day it was passed or made`        IS d
    `what it says about coming into force` IS provision

-- Substituted provisions in an Act passed on 10 March 2026, in force on a particular day, 1 June 2026.
`substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` MEANS `an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (`a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- Substituted provisions in an Act passed on 10 March 2026 that says nothing about its coming into force: section 4(b), 10 March 2026.
`substituted provisions that say nothing` MEANS `an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) `no provision`
-- Substituted provisions whose day is to be fixed later and has not been.
`substituted provisions whose day is not yet fixed` MEANS `an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (`a day to be fixed later` NOTHING)
-- Substituted provisions in subordinate legislation that says nothing about its coming into force.
`substituted provisions in silent subordinate legislation` MEANS `an enactment` `subordinate legislation` (YMD 2026 3 10) `no provision`

§ `Section 2: amendment or repeal in the same Session`

#ASSERT `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2025-26" "2025-26"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2025-26" "2026-27" BECAUSE "section 2 speaks only of the Session in which the Act is passed and says nothing of another Session"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2025-26" "2024-25" BECAUSE "section 2 speaks only of the Session in which the Act is passed and says nothing of another Session"

§ `Section 15: repeal of a repeal`

-- "the repeal does not revive any enactment previously repealed unless words are added reviving it".
#ASSERT `section 15 provides that the repeal of a repealing enactment does not revive the enactment previously repealed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 15 provides that the repeal of a repealing enactment does not revive the enactment previously repealed` TRUE

§ `Section 16(1): general savings`

-- Every one of the five things, without and with a contrary intention.
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `the previous operation of the enactment repealed or anything duly done or suffered under it` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `the previous operation of the enactment repealed or anything duly done or suffered under it` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that the repeal of an enactment by an Act does not revive or affect` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` TRUE

-- The closing words: only investigations, proceedings, remedies, penalties, forfeitures and punishments.
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` TRUE
-- Not named in the closing words: the section does not provide it.
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `the previous operation of the enactment repealed or anything duly done or suffered under it` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 16(1) provides that it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` FALSE

§ `Section 16(2): the expiry of a temporary enactment`

#ASSERT `section 16 treats the way the enactment ceases as a repeal by an Act` `repeal by an Act`
#ASSERT `section 16 treats the way the enactment ceases as a repeal by an Act` `expiry of a temporary enactment`
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 16 treats the way the enactment ceases as a repeal by an Act` `another way` BECAUSE "section 16 speaks only of repeal by an Act and of the expiry of a temporary enactment"

§ `Section 17(1): the repealed enactment remains in force until the substituted provisions come into force`

-- Substituted provisions that name 1 June 2026: in force from the beginning of that day (section 4(a)).
#ASSERT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` (YMD 2026 6 2)
-- The first day of the Act's life and a day a year before.
#ASSERT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` (YMD 2025 6 1)
-- Substituted provisions that say nothing: in force from the beginning of the day of the Royal Assent (section 4(b)).
#ASSERT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that say nothing` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions that say nothing` (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- Where the Act does not substitute provisions, section 17(1) does not apply. The commencement is not asked for, so
-- an unfixed day does not leak a refusal.
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` FALSE `substituted provisions that name 2026-06-01` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` FALSE `substituted provisions whose day is not yet fixed` (YMD 2026 5 31)
-- Where section 4 gives no day for the substituted provisions, neither does section 17(1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions whose day is not yet fixed` (YMD 2026 5 31) BECAUSE "the enactment provides for a day to be fixed later and none is fixed yet, so neither limb of section 4 gives a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE `substituted provisions in silent subordinate legislation` (YMD 2026 5 31) BECAUSE "the Interpretation Act 1978 has no rule on when subordinate legislation that makes no provision comes into force"

§ `Section 17(2): repeal and re-enactment`

`a repeal and re-enactment` MEANS `A re-enactment` WITH
    `the Act repeals and re-enacts a previous enactment, with or without modification` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE

`a repeal and re-enactment with a contrary intention` MEANS `A re-enactment` WITH
    `the Act repeals and re-enacts a previous enactment, with or without modification` IS TRUE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS TRUE

`a repeal without re-enactment` MEANS `A re-enactment` WITH
    `the Act repeals and re-enacts a previous enactment, with or without modification` IS FALSE
    `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE

-- (a) references to the repealed enactment.
#ASSERT `section 17(2)(a) provides that a reference to the repealed enactment is a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a repeal and re-enactment`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2)(a) provides that a reference to the repealed enactment is a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a repeal and re-enactment with a contrary intention`
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2)(a) provides that a reference to the repealed enactment is a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a repeal without re-enactment`
-- (b) things done under the repealed enactment, in so far as they could have been done under the provision re-enacted.
#ASSERT `section 17(2)(b) provides that the subordinate legislation or thing has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a repeal and re-enactment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2)(b) provides that the subordinate legislation or thing has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a repeal and re-enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2)(b) provides that the subordinate legislation or thing has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a repeal and re-enactment with a contrary intention` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 17(2)(b) provides that the subordinate legislation or thing has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a repeal without re-enactment` TRUE
